Only a fresh press counts as a press.

A held button repeats every frame. When an action pops a view, the framework hands focus to whatever
is underneath, and the next repeat then "presses" that by itself: choosing a picture closed the
chooser and the screen below acted on the same button, which left the launcher a screen too far back
with no focus.

--- a/library/lib/application.cpp
+++ b/library/lib/application.cpp
@@ -496,7 +496,10 @@ void Application::onGamepadButtonPressed(char button, bool repeating)
     Application::repetitionOldFocus = Application::currentFocus;
 
     // Actions
-    if (Application::handleAction(button))
+    // Only a fresh press counts: a repeat is for scrolling, never a second press.
+    if (!repeating && Application::handleAction(button))
         return;
 
     // Navigation
